+### Linux packaging
+
+The Linux x64 target packages the same application, runtime, and Web profile as the other targets, with these differences:
+
+- The dsh tree ships without ASAR at `resources/app/dsh`, and the Host, plugins, and the bundled `resources/runtime/cli/bin/dsh` command run it under the bundled primary runtime Node at `resources/runtime/primary-runtime/dependencies/node/bin/node`. Electron's Node links a libvips build that crashes on Linux, so `desktop-runtime.json` records the bundled Node version and the prepared runtime smoke runs against that Node.
+- The package is unsigned and embeds no updater feed or mandatory update policy, because both have Windows and macOS implementations only; install a newer package with the distribution package manager to update.
+- Packaging reads `apps/desktop/.env.linux`, copied from [the Linux template](.env.linux.example), and accepts only shared settings, because the platform has no signing or update-origin fields.
+- Desktop reports the Web client identity to the account service, and installing the terminal `dsh` command into the shell is unsupported.
+- Building the installers requires a Linux x86_64 host with `rpmbuild`, `tar`, `xz`, and `zstd` on `PATH`. The packages include desktop menu entries, icons, and the `dsh://` handler; no FUSE runtime is required.
+
+`pnpm run package:desktop:linux:x64` writes unsigned `.deb`, `.rpm`, and `.pkg.tar.zst` installers under `.desktop-build/targets/linux-x64/artifacts/`, all for x86_64. The RPM uses the v4 package format; the Arch package uses zstd compression. The bundled native libraries require glibc 2.32 or newer. `pnpm run package:desktop:linux:x64:dir` stops at the unpacked application directory. Neither command uploads or tags the commit; Linux updates are distributed as replacement installers.
